      "heading": "What the Critics Say — Limitations of Research on This Supplement Stack for Blood Sugar",
      "body": "<p>While the individual components of the stack have shown promise, the overall evidence base has several limitations. Most studies are short‑term (4–12 weeks) and involve small sample sizes, which limits the ability to detect long‑term safety signals. The heterogeneity of study designs—ranging from single‑arm trials to crossover studies—makes it difficult to pool results. Additionally, many trials did not report on clinically meaningful endpoints such as cardiovascular events or mortality. Another concern is the variability in product quality. Proprietary blends and unverified dosing can lead to inconsistent intake of active ingredients. Finally, the interaction potential with common diabetes medications is not fully understood, especially in patients with complex regimens. > Bottom Line for Skeptics: The stack may offer modest metabolic benefits, but the evidence is still emerging. Long‑term, large‑scale trials are needed to confirm safety and efficacy. Action tip: Consult your healthcare provider before making changes to your routine.</p>\n",
